<title>GERMANY: German state of NRW details November CPI.</title>
<headline>German state of NRW details November CPI.</headline>
<dateline>GERMANY, Frankfurt</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Statistics Office in the west German state of North-Rhine Westphalia gave the following breakdown of its November cost of living data :</p>
<p>						 Percentage change</p>
<p> Index/component			   mth/mth  yr/yr Index</p>
<p> Overall price index		     -0.1     +1.5  114</p>
<p> Prices exc heating oil, fuel	  +0.1     +1.3  113.9</p>
<p> Prices exc seasonal goods	     -0.1     +1.7  114.7</p>
<p> Prices exc services and repairs     +0.1     +1.4  112.7</p>
<p> Rents					 +0.5     +3.4  125.7</p>
<p> Household energy			  +0.1     +2.5  119.8</p>
<p> Personal goods, services and other  -2.2     +0.3  118.9</p>
<p> Transport and communications	  -0.3     +1.8  114.4</p>
<p> Furniture and other household goods  -	 +0.7  111.0</p>
<p> Foodstuffs, drinks, tobacco	   +0.3     +1.2  109.0</p>
<p> Clothing, shoes			   +0.2     +1.1  112.4</p>
<p> Health and personal care items	+0.2     +2.7  114.4</p>
<p> Education, entertainment, leisure   +0.1     +1.0  110.3</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
